    "description": "Developed the Java EE Application Server, JEUS, mainly participating in the backend part of the server.\n\nEJB container, a distributed component container\n- participated in the standardization process (JSR) for EJB\n- as an expert group member, contributed to the new EJB features and its API design\n- added the new EJB features to the application server such as annotaion-based configuration, POJO programming model, dependency injection, transaction management, asynchronous call, timer service, and enhanced remoting service\n\nObject-Relational Mapping (ORM) framework, which provides a persistence layer between plain Java objects and database entities\n- participated in the standardization process (JSR) for JPA\n- participated in open source project GlassFish as a committer\n- contributed to generating SQLs for MySQL and Oracle, JPA QL, caching, logging, and many others [1].\n\nOther contributions\n- contributed to the new features for distributed transaction manager, database connection pools, clustering services, JNDI service registry, and system management.\n- Built continuous testing and build systems using Ant, JUnit, TestNG, and Hudson\n- Contributed to the acquisition of Java EE 5 compatibility certificate\n\nSkills/tools used: Java, C/C++, XML, Servlet, EJB, JPA, RMI, CORBA, SQL, Oracle, MySQL, TCP/IP, JNI, Subversion, JUnit, TestNG, Ant, Maven, Eclipse\n\n[1] http://java.net/jira/secure/IssueNavigator.jspa?jqlQuery=Participants+%3D+guruwons",
